adjudication.rationale:
In `EventManager.createAllCalendarEvents`, the legacy-path for a `destination` without `credentialId` now does:

```ts
const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter(c => c.type === destination.integration);
createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
  await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(async (c) => await createEvent(c, event)))
);
```

But `createEvent` was changed to accept an optional `externalId` and returns it in the `EventResult` (`externalId` is later used to set `externalCalendarId` in booking references via `result.externalId`). Since this branch does not pass `destination.externalId`, the resulting `EventResult.externalId` will be `undefined`, whereas previously the reference used `evt.destinationCalendar?.externalId` (when `destinationCalendar` was a single object) so it would have been preserved.

Therefore, for legacy rows (no `credentialId`), calendar references can lose the external calendar target, impacting subsequent update/delete operations that rely on `externalCalendarId` from the reference. The fix is to pass `destination.externalId` into `createEvent(c, event, destination.externalId)` (or equivalent).
